Add api/src/types/task.ts and api/src/db/tasks.ts with typed functions for task CRUD.

**What/Why:** REQ-032-036 require task operations. Data-access layer provides typed functions for the REST routes.

**Files:**
- `api/src/types/task.ts` (new) — Task interface
- `api/src/db/tasks.ts` (new) — Prepared statements and functions

**Task interface:**
```ts
interface Task {
  id: number;
  project_id: number;
  title: string;
  note: string | null;
  completed: boolean; // converted from INTEGER at boundary
  sort_order: number | null;
  created_at: string;
  updated_at: string;
}
```

**Functions:**
- `createTask(projectId: number, title: string, note?: string): Task`
- `listTasksByProject(projectId: number): Task[]`
- `getTask(id: number): Task | undefined`
- `updateTask(id: number, data: { title?: string; note?: string; completed?: boolean }): Task | undefined`
- `deleteTask(id: number): boolean`
- `countTasksByProject(projectId: number): number`

**Approach:** Use prepared statements with named params. Convert `completed` INTEGER 0/1 to/from boolean at the boundary (read: `!!row.completed`, write: `completed ? 1 : 0`). Update `updated_at` on every updateTask call.

**Tests to run:** `npm run build -w api` compiles cleanly.

**Acceptance:** All 6 functions exist, return typed results, boolean conversion works correctly, build passes.

Add Task types and API client methods to the web app.

**What/Why:** The web app needs typed client methods to call task REST endpoints before building the Redux slice and UI.

**Files:**
- `web/src/api/types.ts` — Add Task and TaskInput interfaces
- `web/src/api/client.ts` — Add task API functions

**Types:**
```ts
interface Task {
  id: number;
  project_id: number;
  title: string;
  note: string | null;
  completed: boolean;
  sort_order: number | null;
  created_at: string;
  updated_at: string;
}

interface TaskInput {
  title: string;
  note?: string | null;
}
```

**Client functions:**
- `fetchTasksByProject(projectId: number): Promise<Task[]>`
- `fetchTask(id: number): Promise<Task>`
- `createTask(projectId: number, data: TaskInput): Promise<Task>`
- `updateTask(id: number, data: Partial<TaskInput> & { completed?: boolean }): Promise<Task>`
- `deleteTask(id: number): Promise<void>`

**Approach:** Follow the same patterns as project client methods. Use correct endpoint paths matching the API routes.

**Tests to run:** `npm run build -w web` compiles cleanly.

**Acceptance:** All types and functions added, TypeScript compiles, paths match API routes.

