Implement light and dark themes with toggle and persistence across reloads.

**What/Why:** REQ-048/AC-048 require theme toggle that persists. Users can choose their preferred appearance.

**Files:**
- `web/src/styles/theme.css` (new) — CSS variables for both themes
- `web/src/features/theme/ThemeToggle.tsx` (new) — Toggle button component
- `web/src/features/theme/useTheme.ts` (new) — Theme hook with persistence
- `web/src/App.tsx` — Apply theme class, render toggle

**CSS variables approach:**
```css
:root, [data-theme='light'] {
  --bg-primary: #ffffff;
  --bg-secondary: #f5f5f7;
  --text-primary: #1d1d1f;
  --text-secondary: #86868b;
  --border-color: #d2d2d7;
  --accent-color: #007aff;
  /* ... more */
}

[data-theme='dark'] {
  --bg-primary: #1c1c1e;
  --bg-secondary: #2c2c2e;
  --text-primary: #f5f5f7;
  /* ... dark equivalents */
}
```

**useTheme hook:**
- Reads initial theme from localStorage (default: 'light' or system preference)
- Provides `theme` value and `toggleTheme` function
- Persists to localStorage on change
- Sets `data-theme` attribute on document.documentElement

**ThemeToggle:**
- Simple button with sun/moon icon or text
- Calls toggleTheme on click
- Place in sidebar header or app header

**Tests to run:** `npm run build -w web`, manual testing: toggle theme, reload, verify persistence.

**Acceptance:** Both themes work, toggle switches immediately, preference persists after reload, all UI elements respect theme variables.
